    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d150">

                <pb facs="0482" n="460" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v2/pg460"/>

                <head>No. 15.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish to General Schenck</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-04-02"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 2,
                        1872</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>We understand the British Government is bound to file Counter-Case, and that
                    their so doing will not prejudice any position they have taken, nor affect any
                    position of this Government. The rights of both parties will be the same after
                    filing as before.</p>
                <p>Is the inquiry made at their request?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>FISH.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
